        "y0": 0.511208282576667,
        "x1": 0.7496064628650939,
        "y1": 0.5237873732441604
      },
      "text": "earlier work by Maslov [10] on resolution calculi for classical predicate logic.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.22647089740030127,
        "y0": 0.5262084043387211,
        "x1": 0.7931337543562347,
        "y1": 0.5387874950062145
      },
      "text": "Mints defines a class of formulas, clauses, with a particularly simple structure",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.20705882552402471,
        "y0": 0.5413599194902362,
        "x1": 0.7913727105832568,
        "y1": 0.5539390101577296
      },
      "text": "(details below). Given a formula ϕ, he constructs a corresponding set of clauses M",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.2070589751199959,
        "y0": 0.5565114346417515,
        "x1": 0.5437253066916871,
        "y1": 0.5690905253092449
      },
      "text": "such that for some designated basic sentence g,",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.441764781677645,
        "y0": 0.5831779795463639,
        "x1": 0.46666702569699753,
        "y1": 0.5957570702138573
      },
      "text": "⊢ ϕ",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.48313794104881536,
        "y0": 0.5831779795463639,
        "x1": 0.497058893340865,
        "y1": 0.5957570702138573
      },
      "text": "iff",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
